    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0448" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4773: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-11T21:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1927—9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 12—1:03 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>131. Following from Stimson:</p>
                <p>“With Minister Eberhardt, Admiral Latimer and General Feland, have had a second
                    conference today with Moncada and one of his generals <pb facs="0449" n="347"
                        xml:id="pg347"/> at Tipitapa. I believe we have concluded satisfactorily the
                    final details for the disarmament of the insurgent army which is expected to be
                    completed in two days after which I am invited to meet personally and address it
                    at Las Banderas on Saturday.”<anchor n="72" xml:id="d328-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
